12 CO DEP-001~ DEP-003 DEP-004 DEP-005 m=M d=MX c=M | Dependency changes follow the add-dependency workflow whose listed content (latest stable compatible version from the registry, deprecation, vulnerability and license checks, approval gates) restates DEP-003/004/005; post-command and post-edit manifest checks with workflow naming are the mechanism (C3).
13 NN rel=DEP-025 | Factual note that the guard's parser is minimal (npx npm, -EncodedCommand not covered): enforcement is narrower than the rule; no behavior imposed.
14 CD DEP-025 m=MN k=W st=S c=M | PreToolUse deny of npm install/ci/install-test/update carrying --force, -f, --legacy-peer-deps, npm_config_* env or npm config of those keys. DEP-025 forbids the flags "merely to bypass incompatible peer dependencies"; the hook denies them regardless of purpose.
  x: the flags/env/config are denied on every install-like npm command regardless of purpose
  s: `npm ci --force` used to force re-fetching packages after cache corruption with compatible peers: not a peer-dependency bypass under DEP-025; M's hook denies it.
15 CD DEP-025 m=MN k=W st=S c=M | The bypass block has no exception path and also applies to setting the npm config key without any install (dependency-guard.mjs:80-82, 106-116).
  x: unconditional deny including `npm config set` of force/legacy-peer-deps without an install
  s: `npm config set legacy-peer-deps false` to restore the safe default: no bypass under DEP-025; denied by the hook (static reading of the config-key match).
16 CD DEP-025 m=MN k=W st=S c=M | Config-key/env match blocks commands touching force/legacy-peer-deps regardless of intent, including read-only `npm config get` and `npm config set force false` (BYPASS_CONFIG_KEY match on positionals, dependency-guard.mjs:81,108-109).
  x: read-only or bypass-disabling npm config commands on those keys are denied
  s: `npm config get legacy-peer-deps` to inspect configuration: nothing bypassed under DEP-025; M's hook denies it (static reading; not executed).
